1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,500
I said free Palestine.

2
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:18,400
I want those words to be loud and clear so the people from Gaza all the way to the occupied West Bank know that we have not forgotten them.

3
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,200
And this next song was inspired.

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:34,400
By the bravery of Columbia University students who led an encampment movement that mobilized the entire world, opened up hearts, myself included.

5
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:41,900
So thank you to those students that risked their diplomas, that risked their tuition, that risked their scholarships, that stood up and said no.

6
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:46,300
To all of my Jewish brothers and sisters.

7
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:56,000
Criticism of Israel, criticism of apartheid, being against genocide in no way is a criticism of you.

8
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,000
So I say free Palestine.

9
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,100
I say free Lebanon.

10
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,500
I say free Cuba.

11
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:11,000
I say free Congo, free Sudan, free all people in America living in fear over this terrorist organization, ICE.
